course: dictionary
lesson: 2888
title: Words hidden in words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dormitory is a large bedroom with many beds, where many people sleep together, such as in a boarding school, camp or hostel. It is a noun, so you can have one dormitory or several dormitories.
explain: «An anagram uses exactly the same letters in a new order: LISTEN becomes SILENT, and DORMITORY becomes DIRTY ROOM.» To check an anagram, count the letters in each word. If the numbers and kinds of letters match, you have an anagram.
explain: «DORMITORY is an anagram of DIRTY ROOM.» The space in DIRTY ROOM does not count as a letter. Both words use the same nine letters, so one is a rearranged version of the other.
fact: A dormitory is a large bedroom with many beds, such as in a boarding school, camp or hostel.
fact: In the US, «dorm» is short for a college or university building where students live.
fact: In the UK, a «dormitory town» is a town where people live but travel elsewhere to work.
fact: An anagram uses exactly the same letters in a new order, so «DORMITORY» and «DIRTY ROOM» are anagrams of each other.
fact: Anagrams are a fun way to spot patterns in words: LISTEN becomes SILENT.
exercise: In a boarding school story, where do the children sleep and have midnight feasts? | In the playground | *In the dormitory | In the science lab | In the library
exercise: «An anagram uses exactly the same letters in a new order.» What is an anagram? | A long word with many syllables | A word that means the opposite of another | A word with a silent letter | *A word made by rearranging the letters of another word
exercise: In the UK, what is a dormitory town? | A town with a famous castle | *A town where people live but travel elsewhere to work | A town that is only for students | A town with no houses at all
test: «DORMITORY is an anagram of DIRTY ROOM.» How many letters are in DIRTY ROOM, not counting the space? | 8 | 7 | 10 | *9
test: In the US, what does «dorm» short for? | *A college building where students live | Door | Dormant | Dome
exam: Which word is NOT an anagram of LISTEN? | TINSEL | *LISTENER | SILENT | ENLIST
